"The table illustrates how many barrels of oil were produced daily in four countries between 2000 and 2004.": "",
"Overall, there was an increase in the daily amount of oil produced in Nigeria, Chad and Somalia, while a gradual decline was seen in Congo.": "",
"In addition, Congo generally produced the most oil among the four countries, but it was overtaken by Nigeria in the final year.": "",
"Daily oil production in Nigeria rose slightly from 205,000 barrels in 2000 to 210,000 barrels in 2001, before falling to 190,000 barrels the following year.": "",
"It then recovered to 213,000 barrels in 2004, the highest figure that year.": "",
"In Chad, oil production stood at zero in the first three years, but it then rose to 8,000 barrels in 2003 and 50,000 barrels in 2004.": "",
"Similarly, Somalia witnessed a steady increase from only 5,000 barrels to 50,000 barrels over the period.": "",
"By contrast, Congo produced the highest output in 2000, at 275,000 barrels, outnumbering its counterparts.": "",
"However, this figure decreased steadily over the next four years and reached 203,000 barrels in 2004.": "",
